      "attempt_id": "B_transitive_attempt_1",
      "message": "lares `CONTRACT_VERSION = 1`, so **v1 semantics** are what got frozen into the artifact. There was no v2 in the committed contract \u2014 it contains only v1, so \"copy v1/v2 semantics\" resolved to v1. If a v2 is later introduced upstream (e.g. allowing `paid \u2192 cancelled`), this artifact will silently keep v1 behaviour; that divergence is deliberate and documented in the module docstring, since the artifact is not allowed to track the contract at runtime.\n\n## Verification performed\n\nRan a five-case check covering both allowed transitions (`new\u2192paid`, `new\u2192cancelled`) and three rejected ones (`paid\u2192new`, `new\u2192new`, `paid\u2192cancelled`), plus the version assertion and an assertion that `semkg_contract` never entered `sys.modules`. All passed.\n\nOne caveat on tooling: `run_command` only permits `python`, and stdout from the interpreter wasn't captured back to me (only exit status), so I converted the check into assertion form so pass/fail was observable via the return code rather than printed text."
    },
